        "title": {
          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Asha picked a number: if even, halve it; if odd, triple it and add 1.\n\"Where does it end?\" she wondered."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "rule",
          "sequence",
          "pattern"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Some sequences are made by a rule applied again and again. Start with 6: 6, 3, 10, 5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1. This is the Collatz rule.\nNobody has proved that every starting number reaches 1, though it works for every number tested.\nPlaying with such rules builds our sense of patterns and proofs."
        }
